sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 12-semantic-cache-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle How litellm-dev decides between replaying a cached answer from Qdrant and calling the model
  %% @type external: BGE GEN
  %% @type database: Q
  actor C as Client
  participant LL as litellm-dev<br/>semantic cache default off
  participant BGE as bge-m3<br/>remote GPU host
  participant Q as Qdrant<br/>tmpfs, end-user scope
  participant GEN as Generation model

  C->>LL: chat completion
  alt cache.use-cache is true
    LL->>BGE: embed the messages
    BGE-->>LL: embedding
    LL->>Q: search in the end-user scope
    Q-->>LL: closest cached response
    alt similarity at least 0.92
      LL-->>C: replay cached response with similarity header
    else below 0.92
      LL->>GEN: call the generation model
      GEN-->>LL: completion
      LL-)Q: store the response (tmpfs)
      LL-->>C: response
    end
  else cache not requested
    LL->>GEN: call the generation model
    GEN-->>LL: completion
    LL-->>C: response, nothing cached
  end
